    {
      "id": "library/10665-69034/blocks/prose-sec-003",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Executive summary",
      "pageStart": 9,
      "pageEnd": 11,
      "target": "../sections/sec-003-executive-summary.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "What is the DQS? The DQS is a flexible toolbox of methods to evaluate different\naspects of the immunization monitoring system at district and health unit (HU) levels.\nImmunization “monitoring” refers to the regular ongoing measurement of the level\nof achievement in vaccination coverage and other immunization system indicators\n(e.g. safety, vaccine management). Monitoring is closely linked with reporting because\nit involves data collection and processing.\nTarget audience. This document is to be used primarily by staff who will adapt the\ntoolbox for a specific area (usually staff at national and",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The executive summary describes the DQS as a flexible toolbox for assessing immunization monitoring systems at district and health unit levels, aimed at national and regional staff who adapt it. It aims to check the accuracy of reported immunization numbers and the quality of monitoring practices, in support of the Reaching Every District approach. Findings are analysed to identify strengths, weaknesses and practical recommendations, with the goal of building the most relevant options into routine practice.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/10665-69034/blocks/prose-sec-004",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "A. Introduction",
      "pageStart": 11,
      "pageEnd": 12,
      "target": "../sections/sec-004-a-introduction.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "1\nIncreasing immunization coverage at the health facility level. Geneva, WHO, 2002 (WHO/V&B/\n02.27). RED is a global strategy aimed at increasing coverage and decreasing drop-out rates. It is a five-\npart strategy: reaching the underserved, providing supportive supervision, increasing use of data for\naction, increasing micro-planning capacity at district levels and using local populations in planning\nimmunization sessions.",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "A footnote describing the Reaching Every District strategy and its five parts, from reaching the underserved to involving local communities in planning sessions.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
